From: =?UTF-8?q?=E4=BB=93=E9=BC=A0=E7=8E=8B?= <yjianbin419@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:05:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] test+feat(agent): honour Idempotency-Key on POST
 agent/commands (ORD-0253 server half)

The route accepted the header and dropped it, so one key could activate two
missions. Reuse the replan/accept vocabulary (validate_idempotency_key,
canonical_request_signature, the idempotency_keys receipt row and its canonical
409) behind an operation-scoped key agent.command:<key>: a replay returns the
one persisted mission, a same-key different-intent request fails closed instead
of silently aliasing, and a keyless caller behaves exactly as before.

10 doors; 4 reverse-mutation arms (per-call regenerated key, constant signature,
dropped operation scope, skipped validation) each redden their named cell and
are restored byte-exact. Contract declares the same header name/schema, with
requiredness as the only difference.
